*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* CALL !SETTZ(zone)
*
* Sets the private configuration parameter TIMEZONE of this process, the zone the epoch functions MVDATE(), MVTIME(),
* MVDATE.TIME() and MVEPOCH() use.  Equivalent to CONFIG TIMEZONE zone.  A null string goes back to the process's own TZ.
* A zone this machine does not have is refused and leaves the setting as it was: STATUS() is 2, as for a refused CONFIG.
* ($internal because PCONFIG is: a user program reaches it only through the SET.TIMEZONE statement.)
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine settz(zone)
$catalog !settz

   if pconfig('TIMEZONE', zone) then null
   return
end

* END-CODE
